    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Brady House** headlining the offensive unit. **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our highest-rated start at 68.57, bolstered by a prime leadoff spot and a +14% boost from a favorable right-handed platoon matchup against Meyer. Similarly, **Brady House** (63.19) provides high utility value against Woods Richardson; the favorable SP xERA of 4.85 for the opposing starter, paired with a significant +19% SP skill advantage, makes him an excellent play for run production. While **Jackson Merrill** (60.00) faces a tougher L-on-L matchup against Liberatore, his leadoff placement and strong underlying projections keep him in the \"Strong\" start tier, ensuring we maximize our top-of-order exposure.\n\nOur primary bench decision centered on **Coby Mayo**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 37.37. While **Coby Mayo** profiles as a high-upside asset, the combination of a daunting matchup against the elite 3.69 xERA of Meyer and a low batting order position (#8) pushed him below our 40.0 efficiency floor, forcing us to prioritize lineup stability. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while the bench also sits quiet today due to scheduled off-days for core contributors **Kyle Tucker** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** \n\nManagement is closely monitoring **Liam Hicks** (40.61) today, as his projection remains precarious due to a -11% penalty from a dynamic platoon disadvantage against Povich. While he holds the lineup #3 spot, the matchup risk makes him the most volatile piece in the current configuration. With **Nasim Nunez** (59.76) providing critical speed potential despite hitting in the #9 hole, the Waves are prioritizing efficiency over raw power to navigate this slate, assuming our projected order holds as the daily lineups finalize.",
